Song Title: I Stand Amazed (How Marvellous)
Artist / Author:
Writers: Charles Hutchinson Gabriel, Chris Tomlin
Release year:
CCLI song #: 4674207
Order: Verse 1, Chorus, Verse 2, Chorus, Verse 3, Chorus, Chorus

Verse 1
I stand amazed in the presence
Of Jesus the Nazarene
And wonder how He could love me
A sinner condemned, unclean

Chorus
(Singin’) How marvellous, how wonderful
And my song shall ever be
How marvellous, how wonderful
Is my Saviour’s love for me

Verse 2
He took my sins and my sorrows
He made them His very own
He bore the burden to Calvary
And suffered and died alone

Chorus
(Singin’) How marvellous, how wonderful
And my song shall ever be
How marvellous, how wonderful
Is my Saviour’s love for me

Verse 3
And with the ransomed in glory
His face I at last shall see
’Twill be my joy through the ages
To sing of His love for me

Chorus
(Singin’) How marvellous, how wonderful
And my song shall ever be
How marvellous, how wonderful
Is my Saviour’s love for me

Chorus
(Singin’) How marvellous, how wonderful
And my song shall ever be
How marvellous, how wonderful
Is my Saviour’s love for me
